# MIME types.
#
# Hostinger's default map is missing many modern extensions and falls back to
# text/plain for them. That is not just a cosmetic mislabel: a text/* response
# gets gzipped, and a compressed response cannot serve byte ranges, so audio
# and video silently lose seeking. This file pins the correct type for every
# format likely to be served here.
#
# Syntax per Hostinger docs (support article 1583371): "AddType type/subtype ext"
# -- extensions are listed WITHOUT a leading dot, and directives are NOT wrapped
# in <IfModule>, because LiteSpeed does not register Apache module names and a
# guarded block would be silently skipped.

# Audio
AddType audio/mp4 m4a m4b f4a f4b
AddType audio/aac aac
AddType audio/flac flac
AddType audio/ogg ogg oga opus
AddType audio/wav wav
AddType audio/webm weba
AddType audio/midi mid midi

# Video
AddType video/mp4 mp4 m4v f4v f4p
AddType video/webm webm
AddType video/ogg ogv
AddType video/quicktime mov
AddType video/x-matroska mkv

# Subtitles and captions
AddType text/vtt vtt

# Images
AddType image/webp webp
AddType image/avif avif
AddType image/svg+xml svg svgz
AddType image/heic heic
AddType image/heif heif
AddType image/x-icon ico

# Fonts
AddType font/woff woff
AddType font/woff2 woff2
AddType font/ttf ttf
AddType font/otf otf
AddType application/vnd.ms-fontobject eot

# Web application
AddType text/javascript js mjs
AddType application/json json
AddType application/manifest+json webmanifest
AddType application/wasm wasm

# Documents and archives
AddType application/epub+zip epub
AddType application/zip zip
AddType application/gzip gz
AddType text/markdown md
